WEBVTT

01:31.800 --> 01:34.427
Ionic nitrate…

01:35.011 --> 01:36.846
So, it's the nitric acid…

01:43.728 --> 01:47.690
Oh… Just as I thought you'd be, Stan,

01:47.774 --> 01:50.193
the one to wake up right after me.

01:57.367 --> 02:00.995
How long has it been?

02:01.079 --> 02:04.457
I'd say it's been
at least a few thousand years.

02:04.541 --> 02:06.668
There are no buildings.

02:06.751 --> 02:10.130
For the rebars to weather away,
the concrete's pH has to--

02:10.213 --> 02:11.798
Okay, I get it.

02:12.423 --> 02:13.967
You don't have to tell me…

02:17.887 --> 02:21.349
Even our clothes rotted away, Stan.

02:21.432 --> 02:23.768
There's no way your cigarettes
would still be there.

02:25.728 --> 02:30.024
This is a good chance
for you to stop smoking.

02:32.735 --> 02:36.531
So, what do we do now?

02:36.614 --> 02:39.200
Like a man once said,

02:40.827 --> 02:42.912
no matter what circumstances
humanity faces,

02:43.496 --> 02:46.291
<i>there will always be</i>
<i>someone willing to discover</i>

02:46.374 --> 02:48.126
<i>how this world works.</i>

02:49.752 --> 02:51.671
So this is now a contest.

02:52.380 --> 02:55.508
Quite an elegant contest, I must say.

02:56.092 --> 02:58.970
Whoever masters science the fastest

02:59.053 --> 03:02.557
will become the dictator
of this Stone World.

03:07.604 --> 03:12.442
ORIGINAL WORK: RIICHIRO INAGAKI, BOICHI
SHUEISHA JUMP COMICS

04:46.327 --> 04:47.412
What is this?

04:47.996 --> 04:51.040
It's a low-concentration nitric acid.

04:51.124 --> 04:54.627
This will wake them up.

04:55.211 --> 04:58.131
I explained it
a few thousand years ago, too.

04:58.631 --> 05:01.884
When the swallow stone statues were
scrubbed with nitric acid glass wool--

05:01.968 --> 05:04.137
Okay, I get it.

05:04.762 --> 05:09.058
As long as they heeded
the "stay conscious" command,

05:09.142 --> 05:10.852
they should be fine, right?

05:18.401 --> 05:21.654
Special Forces Superheroes, assemble!

05:21.738 --> 05:23.948
Despite of being told to stay awake,

05:24.032 --> 05:25.450
only we remain!

05:26.159 --> 05:27.452
Only we survived…

05:27.535 --> 05:30.079
No, only we woke up!

05:30.163 --> 05:32.707
Each person wakes up at their own time,

05:32.790 --> 05:35.960
so the others could revive at any moment.

05:36.044 --> 05:41.799
I believe the venue staff around us
also heard Stan's order,

05:41.883 --> 05:45.178
so there's a chance
they could wake up too.

05:45.261 --> 05:47.472
No, I bet that's almost impossible.

05:47.555 --> 05:49.474
They were only average people.

05:52.810 --> 05:54.145
My lady!

06:09.368 --> 06:10.495
A ring?

06:11.871 --> 06:14.957
Awesome! Not a single dent on it.

06:15.041 --> 06:17.126
It's because it was preserved

06:17.210 --> 06:20.254
in his stone mouth for millennia,
like a time capsule.

06:28.888 --> 06:31.557
This is… platinum!

06:33.226 --> 06:37.063
Wonderful! It's actually elegant!

06:39.941 --> 06:43.069
<i>For example, if someone like</i>
<i>the Martial Arts World Champion</i>

06:43.152 --> 06:47.865
<i>were the only one</i>
<i>to wake up in this Stone World,</i>

06:47.949 --> 06:51.244
<i>the whole world would soon be his.</i>

06:51.327 --> 06:54.664
However, with just a bit of platinum,

06:54.747 --> 06:58.918
we could produce
huge amounts of nitric acid

06:59.001 --> 07:02.839
and get as much gunpowder as we want.

07:04.215 --> 07:07.593
We'll need a workforce for that purpose.

07:16.561 --> 07:20.189
After we have
a certain amount of personnel

07:20.273 --> 07:23.484
we'll move on to getting Yellow Dent next.

07:24.068 --> 07:27.238
<i>After we've found</i>
<i>a proper place to cultivate corn</i>

07:27.321 --> 07:29.490
<i>we'll establish our base there.</i>

07:38.708 --> 07:41.586
<i>Along with securing</i>
<i>provisions and clothing,</i>

07:41.669 --> 07:43.588
<i>we'll launch a gunpowder factory.</i>

07:44.839 --> 07:47.925
<i>We'll refine metals</i>

07:48.009 --> 07:50.803
<i>and improve precision machine tools</i>
<i>at the same time…</i>

07:54.557 --> 07:57.727
<i>and thus, produce our firearms.</i>

08:08.488 --> 08:10.198
How elegant!

08:10.281 --> 08:13.576
Thus, we've become the greatest scientific

08:13.659 --> 08:16.370
and military force in the Stone World.

08:16.454 --> 08:17.288
Yes.

08:27.006 --> 08:30.426
Oh, so you've noticed that devilish fruit…

08:31.552 --> 08:34.388
There's tobacco growing around this area.

08:36.682 --> 08:40.019
Well, I'll take it then,

08:40.102 --> 08:41.771
as a bonus.

08:44.649 --> 08:46.609
<i>Nicotiana tabacum.</i>

08:47.318 --> 08:50.404
<i>The leaves of the plant are dried</i>

08:50.488 --> 08:52.490
<i>and cut into small pieces.</i>

08:52.573 --> 08:56.994
<i>After rolling them up on paper,</i>
<i>we obtain a cigarette.</i>

09:16.097 --> 09:18.641
<i>Nobody will intimidate me anymore.</i>

09:19.225 --> 09:21.143
<i>With the power of my science</i>

09:21.727 --> 09:25.106
and your gun skills, Stanley,

09:25.189 --> 09:27.650
my childhood friend,

09:28.234 --> 09:31.445
we'll become this world's
ultimate dictators!

09:31.529 --> 09:34.073
We're the ones who can accomplish that.

09:34.156 --> 09:37.076
Don't you think so, Stan?

09:41.038 --> 09:44.083
Yes… Definitely.

09:53.884 --> 09:56.012
So, Senku and Xeno,

09:56.095 --> 09:59.390
former master and apprentice
who woke up around the same time,

09:59.473 --> 10:01.309
set their sights on the same nitric acid.

10:02.476 --> 10:05.396
<i>One of them used it to revive,</i>

10:06.564 --> 10:10.109
<i>while the other used it to kill,</i>
<i>both scientifically.</i>

10:10.693 --> 10:12.069
So that's how it is…

10:18.743 --> 10:21.329
<i>What are they talking about?</i>

10:21.412 --> 10:23.581
<i>That somehow cool guy, Senku…</i>

10:23.664 --> 10:26.876
<i>Is he an acquaintance of Xeno?</i>

10:31.672 --> 10:34.383
<i>I need to approach him casually.</i>

10:34.467 --> 10:37.637
<i>Yes, I'm Luna, the cool woman-</i>

10:37.720 --> 10:39.180
What do you mean?

10:39.889 --> 10:42.391
The doctor who taught us
how to build our rocket

10:42.475 --> 10:45.478
is also the enemy scientist boss?

10:45.561 --> 10:47.396
<i>He's on the deck!</i>

10:47.480 --> 10:51.400
<i>Over there, right now, it's Dr. Taiju!</i>

10:53.069 --> 10:56.572
<i>When I point him out,</i>

10:57.281 --> 10:59.533
<i>Stanley will shoot him down,</i>

10:59.617 --> 11:01.911
<i>and victory will be ours.</i>

11:03.454 --> 11:04.955
<i>Yes…</i>

11:05.039 --> 11:09.126
<i>Of course, this has been my objective.</i>

11:09.210 --> 11:12.671
<i>I'm Luna, the mighty woman…</i>

11:23.682 --> 11:27.645
I'm grateful to a ridiculous extent
that I got this information out of Luna.

11:28.229 --> 11:30.231
If Dr. Xeno

11:30.314 --> 11:35.611
is our enemy,
the Medusa might become our trump card.

11:37.029 --> 11:40.241
Wait, can we still use that?

11:40.324 --> 11:43.536
Well, the battery is long dead.
You already know that.

11:43.619 --> 11:44.870
What do you mean?

11:45.663 --> 11:50.042
Dr. Xeno knows very well
the power of scientific weapons.

11:50.126 --> 11:53.629
And he's the type to use them
to dominate the New World.

11:53.712 --> 11:57.675
There's no way he'll ignore
a super-scientific weapon like Medusa.

11:59.510 --> 12:01.053
I see!

12:01.137 --> 12:04.306
The thing is, it's not about
whether we can actually use it or not.

12:04.390 --> 12:07.268
Since our enemy is a skilled scientist,

12:07.351 --> 12:11.814
it can be used as a bluff card
for an invincible, ultimate weapon.

12:11.897 --> 12:13.607
Exactly.

12:14.942 --> 12:18.279
I don't get it. Can we really use
the Medusa, which has no battery,

12:18.362 --> 12:20.448
to intimidate the enemy?

12:20.531 --> 12:24.452
<i>This is my chance to point out Dr. Taiju!</i>

12:25.119 --> 12:27.246
<i>I just need to move my finger, right?</i>

12:27.329 --> 12:29.373
<i>Yes, it's easy. It'll be over!</i>

12:29.457 --> 12:32.168
<i>Cold yet cool, here it goes…</i>

13:09.872 --> 13:13.584
Let's treat her injuries in the back!

13:30.267 --> 13:31.560
<i>I can't!</i>

13:36.690 --> 13:39.068
<i>It wasn't supposed to be like this,</i>

13:39.151 --> 13:42.947
<i>even though I'm a cool, mighty woman…</i>

13:43.030 --> 13:45.533
<i>At least I've got to</i>
<i>transmit the information I have.</i>

13:48.410 --> 13:51.080
<i>There's someone</i>
<i>who could be Xeno's acquaintance.</i>

13:51.163 --> 13:53.082
<i>A guy called Senku…</i>

13:55.167 --> 13:57.211
My lady's saying something.

13:57.294 --> 13:58.462
Huh?

13:59.129 --> 14:02.716
"Sen…ku…"

14:02.800 --> 14:05.219
"Sen…ku…"

14:11.934 --> 14:15.688
"Sen…ku…" What is she talking about?

14:15.771 --> 14:17.022
I have no idea.

14:17.106 --> 14:20.234
But my lady risked her life
to obtain that info.

14:20.317 --> 14:21.819
I'm sure it's important.

14:21.902 --> 14:24.071
It's time to report to Xeno!

14:27.449 --> 14:29.577
<i>White Castle, White Castle.</i>

14:29.660 --> 14:31.871
<i>This is Ghost 2 speaking.</i>

14:31.954 --> 14:34.748
<i>I'm relaying information from Goddess.</i>

14:40.921 --> 14:41.922
What?

14:42.798 --> 14:43.632
Senku!

14:47.511 --> 14:48.596
What is it?

14:48.679 --> 14:52.516
<i>I was setting up the radio</i>
<i>for regular broadcasts</i>

14:52.600 --> 14:55.060
<i>when I picked up this weird noise!</i>

15:00.149 --> 15:01.942
A scramble?

15:03.777 --> 15:06.697
<i>This is certainly</i>
<i>an encrypted communication.</i>

15:06.780 --> 15:11.160
Encrypted, as in talking in secret?
How cunning!

15:11.243 --> 15:12.202
Is it Xeno?

15:12.286 --> 15:14.914
Is it possible to decipher it?

15:14.997 --> 15:18.876
It's not that easy.
We'd need a spectrum analyzer.

15:18.959 --> 15:22.838
I don't really know what that is,
but can't we get one right away?

15:23.464 --> 15:26.800
<i>The details of the conversation</i>
<i>are not that important.</i>

15:27.843 --> 15:31.180
<i>Luna was communicating</i>
<i>by making some gestures.</i>

15:32.431 --> 15:34.016
<i>That means…</i>

15:35.684 --> 15:38.562
<i>the enemies are lurking nearby!</i>

15:51.951 --> 15:56.080
Okay, here you are, Dr. Taiju…

15:59.625 --> 16:00.876
Don't shoot, Stan!

16:06.048 --> 16:08.550
Dr. Taiju was a decoy.

16:10.094 --> 16:12.012
<i>The enemies' actual leader…</i>

16:13.055 --> 16:15.015
<i>is a skilled scientist named…</i>

16:17.393 --> 16:18.602
Senku.

16:19.853 --> 16:22.481
It's Senku Ishigami.

16:24.817 --> 16:26.235
Well…

16:26.819 --> 16:30.239
So which one is our real guy?

16:30.322 --> 16:32.074
<i>That Dr. Senku?</i>

16:35.160 --> 16:38.789
<i>The first man to answer the phone</i>
<i>way back then…</i>

16:38.872 --> 16:40.916
<i>Do you copy me, Perseus?</i>

16:41.000 --> 16:43.127
<i>There's been a small change in our plans--</i>

16:43.210 --> 16:45.713
<i>Okay, that's enough. Stop talking.</i>

16:46.839 --> 16:49.800
<i>That split-second scientific judgement…</i>

16:52.845 --> 16:54.888
<i>Perhaps I could infer something</i>

16:54.972 --> 16:56.849
<i>from the countless discussions</i>

16:56.932 --> 16:59.143
<i>about rockets we had</i>
<i>a few thousand years ago.</i>

16:59.226 --> 17:01.311
<i>His personality, his tone…</i>

17:02.938 --> 17:05.232
<i>Every phone call had been recorded.</i>

17:06.608 --> 17:08.610
Senku's voice…

17:09.945 --> 17:11.613
…is this one!

17:12.239 --> 17:15.909
Of course I can't hear his voice
from this far away.

17:15.993 --> 17:17.286
<i>There's no need to.</i>

17:18.245 --> 17:20.998
I can estimate his height
just by hearing a bit of his voice.

17:23.667 --> 17:26.628
<i>I'll calculate the vocal tract length</i>
<i>ratio from the range</i>

17:26.712 --> 17:28.630
<i>of the smoothing function's domain.</i>

17:28.714 --> 17:31.133
<i>If applied to the average human height,</i>

17:31.216 --> 17:33.302
<i>he should be about 5 feet 7 inches,</i>

17:33.385 --> 17:35.471
<i>with an error margin of one or two inches.</i>

17:36.722 --> 17:40.893
<i>Besides, since that first</i>
<i>and last time we met,</i>

17:40.976 --> 17:44.271
<i>he is probably much taller,</i>
<i>but certainly not much shorter..</i>

17:47.983 --> 17:49.276
<i>In other words…</i>

17:50.652 --> 17:53.572
<i>At 5 feet, 7 to 8 inches tall,</i>

17:53.655 --> 17:56.033
<i>we're looking for a 19-year-old male.</i>

17:56.784 --> 17:59.828
Okay, that's enough.

18:01.538 --> 18:05.751
I can tell his height right away
by comparing him to Luna's size.

18:08.087 --> 18:09.379
One…

18:11.757 --> 18:12.966
Two…

18:15.594 --> 18:18.722
There are three people who qualify.

18:19.348 --> 18:21.308
A sniper! There's a sniper!

18:22.476 --> 18:24.937
Take cover behind something!

18:36.949 --> 18:38.534
<i>They found us out?</i>

18:39.284 --> 18:41.286
<i>Fool! Don't look at me, Luna.</i>

18:41.995 --> 18:43.831
<i>You'll expose the sniper!</i>

18:45.332 --> 18:48.252
<i>No, wait… Look at me!</i>

18:49.753 --> 18:51.713
<i>Who's the skilled scientist leader,</i>

18:51.797 --> 18:55.092
<i>the hot-headed guy among these three?</i>

18:55.175 --> 18:58.971
<i>If the target's</i>
<i>as hot-headed as Xeno says,</i>

18:59.054 --> 19:04.518
<i>he'll certainly follow your gaze, Luna,</i>
<i>and then look at me</i>

19:04.601 --> 19:05.894
<i>instinctively…</i>

19:07.396 --> 19:09.314
<i>He'll be flushed out.</i>

19:09.398 --> 19:12.693
<i>Hi, Senku Ishigami.</i>

19:20.951 --> 19:23.120
<i>He's beyond the line of fire.</i>

19:27.332 --> 19:28.625
Master Senku!

19:31.920 --> 19:35.340
<i>He's run to a geometrically optimal point.</i>

19:35.424 --> 19:36.758
<i>Not bad.</i>

19:37.634 --> 19:42.264
<i>But right because of that, I can see you.</i>

19:43.974 --> 19:46.268
Xeno, I'm going to ask you

19:46.894 --> 19:48.270
one last time.

19:50.230 --> 19:55.027
<i>Are you sure you want me to kill him?</i>

20:04.328 --> 20:07.206
I'll dominate this world with my science.

20:08.290 --> 20:10.125
<i>Perhaps I could achieve that</i>

20:10.209 --> 20:13.712
<i>if I could get you on board</i>
<i>so we could work together.</i>

20:15.297 --> 20:21.511
<i>But a future where Senku accepts that</i>
<i>will never come, right?</i>

20:39.988 --> 20:42.908
Go ahead. Do it.

20:55.671 --> 20:57.172
<i>The potato starch…</i>

20:57.256 --> 21:00.592
<i>It's the kudzu we'd used</i>
<i>to make the soft serve.</i>

21:00.676 --> 21:03.971
<i>It's basically the same. I'll add water…</i>

21:34.293 --> 21:36.461
<i>A dilatant fluid…</i>

21:36.545 --> 21:40.632
<i>I made one by mixing a liquid</i>
<i>with powder particles.</i>

21:41.466 --> 21:45.512
<i>When moved gently,</i>
<i>it behaves like a normal fluid.</i>

21:46.763 --> 21:50.851
<i>But when struck with sudden force,</i>
<i>it acts like a solid.</i>

21:50.934 --> 21:56.898
<i>I'm going to discover if I can use that</i>
<i>to make it work as a bulletproof vest.</i>

21:58.650 --> 22:00.986
<i>Though it hasn’t been put</i>
<i>to practical use yet!</i>

23:53.348 --> 23:55.934
NEXT EPISODE

23:56.017 --> 23:57.769
THIS WORK OF FICTION FEATURES ORGANISMS,
MATERIAL AND PROCESSES BASED ON REAL LIFE.

23:57.853 --> 23:59.646
COLLECTING OR REPLICATING THEM
MAY BE DANGEROUS AND ILLEGAL,

23:59.729 --> 24:00.939
SO DO NOT ATTEMPT.

24:01.022 --> 24:01.940
Subtitle translation by: Silvia
